/**
 * @defgroup StarBASE StarBASE — Base VMC Application Classes
 * @brief Foundational callback layer and geometry-QA maker for GEANT3/VMC simulation.
 *
 * StarBASE provides:
 * - A generic VMC application (`StVMCApplication`) in which every lifecycle
 *   callback is delegated to a swappable `GCall` functor.
 * - A particle-transport stack (`StMCStack`) implementing `TVirtualMCStack`.
 * - A full-featured stepping action (`StMCStepping`) that accumulates
 *   radiation-length and absorption-length distributions per TGeo volume.
 * - Geometry loading (`StMCConstructGeometry`), primary generation
 *   (`StMCSimplePrimaryGenerator`), and application bootstrapping
 *   (`StMCInitApp`) hooks.
 * - The `StarBASE` StMaker that drives η-φ geometry-scan runs from the
 *   STAR chain.
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @class GCall
 * @brief Abstract base class for all VMC action hooks.
 *
 * GCall (derives from TNamed) is the universal callback type used by
 * StVMCApplication.  Concrete subclasses override Fun(), FunDD(), or
 * Field() and are invoked through operator()().  A GCall holds cached
 * pointers to the TVirtualMC, TVirtualMCApplication, and TVirtualMCStack
 * set via SetInterfaces(), making them available inside Fun() without
 * relying on global state.
 */

/**
 * @class StVMCApplication
 * @brief Generic TVirtualMCApplication implemented via GCall callbacks.
 *
 * Each TVirtualMCApplication lifecycle method (ConstructGeometry,
 * InitGeometry, GeneratePrimaries, BeginEvent, BeginPrimary, PreTrack,
 * Stepping, PostTrack, FinishPrimary, FinishEvent, Field) is stored as a
 * GCall* and invoked when the MC engine calls the corresponding virtual.
 * Callbacks are registered with SetConstructGeometry(), SetStepping(), etc.
 * Init() runs the mInit callback and propagates the debug level to
 * TGeant3TGeo.  Trig(n) calls gMC->ProcessRun(n).  Field() falls back to
 * a 5 kG uniform field along z when no field callback is registered.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCStack
 * @brief TVirtualMCStack implementation for StarBASE geometry scans.
 *
 * Uses a TObjArray (all tracks) plus a std::stack (tracks pending
 * transport).  PushTrack() creates a StarMCParticle, links mother-daughter
 * TRef chains, and applies a rapidity cut |pz/e| < tanh(6.3) to primaries.
 * PopNextTrack() services the GEANT3 transport loop.
 * PopPrimaryForTracking() gives primary tracks to GEANT3 by index.
 * Clear() deletes all particles and resets counters.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCStepping
 * @brief Per-step material-budget accumulator and histogram filler.
 *
 * Derives from GCall; Fun() is registered as the Stepping callback of
 * StVMCApplication.  At each simulation step, Fun() classifies the step
 * using the SteppingCase and SteppingKaze enumerations, then:
 * - On track entry: records the accumulated radiation length at the entry
 *   point and fills hRadlenAccu1D for all ancestor volumes.
 * - On track exit: accumulates the fractional radiation length for all
 *   volumes in the current TGeo branch and fills per-volume z/r/phi
 *   histograms.
 * - Fills global 2D r-z histograms (h_radlen_rz, h_abslen_rz,
 *   h_pathlen_rz, h_distance_rz, h_ncount_rz) at every step.
 * postTrack() fills per-volume 1D eta histograms at end-of-track.
 * BookHistograms() and bookVolume() allocate the histogram containers
 * indexed by TGeo volume number.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCConstructGeometry
 * @brief GCall that loads and registers the STAR TGeo geometry.
 *
 * Fun() resolves the path ${STAR}/StarDb/VmcGeometry/Geometry.<tag>.C,
 * loads it, calls CreateTable(), sets CAVE as the top volume, and calls
 * gMC->SetRootGeometry().  If gGeoManager already exists the load step is
 * skipped and the existing geometry is used.  The geometry tag (e.g.
 * "y2023") is the GCall name, passed to the constructor.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCPrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Abstract GCall base for primary-particle generators.
 *
 * Stores track count (fNTrk), PDG code (fPDG), and vertex (fVtx[3]).
 * Provides a PushTrack() helper that forwards to
 * gMC->GetStack()->PushTrack() with the full GEANT3 signature.
 * Subclasses override Fun() and call PushTrack() to populate the stack.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCSimplePrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Uniform-phase-space primary generator.
 *
 * Generates fNTrk particles per event drawn uniformly from configurable
 * pT, eta, phi, and z-vertex windows.  The particle species is given as a
 * Geant3 code (option="G") or a PDG code.  Fun() randomises the z-vertex
 * and calls GenerateOnePrimary() repeatedly.  SetGenerator() and
 * SetVertex() allow run-time reconfiguration without reconstructing the
 * object, which is used by StarBASE::Make() to scan the eta-phi grid.
 */

/**
 * @class StMCInitApp
 * @brief GCall that bootstraps a complete standalone VMC application.
 *
 * When Fun() is invoked (as the mInit callback of StVMCApplication):
 * creates TGeant3TGeo, StMCConstructGeometry, and StMCSimplePrimaryGenerator;
 * registers them; assigns an StMCStack to gMC; calls gMC->Init() and
 * BuildPhysics(); then configures all hadronic and electromagnetic processes
 * to zero with continuous ionisation loss only — the standard geantino
 * configuration for material-budget scanning.
 */

/**
 * @class StarBASE
 * @brief StMaker that orchestrates STAR detector geometry QA scans.
 *
 * Init() creates StVMCApplication, StMCInitApp, and StMCStepping.
 * Make() reads the eta/phi scan grid from maker attributes and calls
 * gMC->ProcessEvent() for each grid cell, reconfiguring the simple
 * generator between calls.  Finish() registers all StMCStepping material-
 * budget histograms into the maker's output dataset.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
